        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.097,
            0.472,
            0.115
          ],
          "content": "Threads of Curiosity"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.125,
            0.587,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": "A tone is a sound of a single frequency like that produced by a tuning fork or by oral whistling (Fig. 10.25a). A musical note like the sound produced by plucking a tanpura string or singing (Fig. 10.25b) is a combination of a lowest frequency called the fundamental and higher frequencies called overtones, which together create a rich and pleasant sound. Indian string instruments like the sarangi, sitar, and veena often use extra strings to enrich this combination."
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.643,
            0.133,
            0.854,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
