        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.6,
            0.473,
            0.619
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Threads of Curiosity"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.632,
            0.657,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "Indian drums like the tabla (Fig. 10.26) or mridangam have a black patch at the centre of the drum head membrane called the syaahi. This patch alters the vibration of the membrane, allowing these instruments to produce a rich variety of sounds. The syaahi also gives a level of tonal control rarely found in other drums."
        },
        {
